  "recommendation": {
    "candidate": "In the existing premium-theme.css body foundation rule add font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums. Follow with :where(button, input, select, textarea, option, optgroup) { font-variant-numeric: inherit; } in the same foundation block. Preserve existing positive numeric rules.",
    "selectorsRationale": "body provides inherited defaults for unclassified table cells, prose containing numeric dates/capacity/runtime, metrics, comparison rows and newly rendered dialogs. Explicit native-control inheritance defeats any user-agent font shorthand resetting inherited numeric variants without changing control family, size, weight, appearance or behavior. option/optgroup included for popup numeric choices; native picker internals remain platform-dependent.",
    "authorShorthandFinding": "Every authored CSS font shorthand in the three loaded stylesheets is font: inherit. They inherit numeric variants; there is no current non-inherit authored shorthand requiring a concrete numeric exception.",
    "resetFinding": "No authored numeric normal/proportional reset exists in this stylesheet inventory.",
    "avoid": "No universal * rule, !important, numeric text replacement, number formatting change, monospace blanket replacement or six-surface-only patch. Do not change font-family/size/weight/line-height to obtain tabular behavior.",
    "exceptions": "No present semantic exception to tabular digits is established by source. Existing Georgia metric/day faces and mono code/raw-match/archive-confirmation faces stay unchanged; feature support depends on installed font. Do not claim equal-width shaping from computed CSS alone."
  },
